{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b4cxvvjvj","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SgqzxLXaepPeGD6gxq7zJP","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-PEHJS9/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-HArM1X/9a675958-8a5c-4163-983a-1ededba583e3/tasks/b4cxvvjvj.output","summary":"Background command \"Run Phase C error-path tests\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"f86594f0-f37d-4cdd-9547-e2bd9c2e65bd","session_id":"9a675958-8a5c-4163-983a-1ededba583e3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_a4jdd5hiz5xu4kxvkqjiomikql7czc53qgwtil7mti4hwxzeghaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte. No fixes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.**\n\n## Scope\nThe library is one C translation unit: `flip_horizontal(cp_image_t*)` (which, despite its name, swaps *rows* — the Rust replicates that, not a \"fixed\" version).\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly 1 symbol (`flip_horizontal`); Rust `.so` exports it with the same name. `nm -D` diff is **empty**; all Rust undefined symbols are libc/libunwind. No C module was left untranslated.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 12 rows. The C has *zero* explicit error handling (no `return`, `assert`, null/range check, or enum), so the surface is the implicit one: `h∈{0,1}`, `h<0`, `h==INT_MIN`, `w==0`, `w<0`, NULL `img`, NULL `pix`, undersized buffer, `int` overflow in row offsets.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 23 rows over 10 branch axes (h parity/sign/magnitude, w magnitude/sign, stride, per-channel content, row adjacency, involution, alignment).\n\n## Results\n| Phase | Tests | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| B (valid paths) | 24 | pass — all 23 `CONFIGS.md` rows |\n| C (error paths) | 13 | pass — all `ERRORS.md` rows |\n| D (symbol parity) | 5 | pass — ELF `.dynsym` parse + `nm -D` + `dlsym` + anti-stub check |\n| Feature combos | default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` | pass (crate declares no `[features]`) |\n| Binary/driver | n/a | neither project builds an executable — no stdout to diff |\n\nBoth libraries are loaded via `libloading`; the Rust is **never** called directly, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test. Each call compares the full allocation (payload + 4 KiB canaries either side), the 16-byte `cp_image_t` struct, and an independent reference model, over randomized inputs (fixed seed). Fatal cases (NULL `img`/`pix`) run in re-spawned child processes and compare `WTERMSIG` — both die with SIGSEGV (139).\n\n## Harness self-check\n`tools/negative_control.sh` builds 10 deliberately broken copies of `lib.rs` — **all 10 are caught**, so the suite genuinely discriminates.\n\nTwo notes on limits I found and handled honestly:\n- `ERRORS.md` E10 (`int` overflow of `w*(h-i-1)` *with* a dereference) is unobservable without >8 GiB of writes. Instead of faking it, I confirmed statically that both use a 32-bit `imul` + sign-extend (`cltq` in C, `movslq` in Rust) before scaling by 4 — a mutant using 64-bit math is documented as semantically equivalent, not a gap.\n- E11 (out-of-range enum) is N/A: the API has no enum/flag parameter. The equivalent \"any `int` is accepted\" surface is covered by a 13×13 boundary cross-product plus 2000 random 32-bit patterns in `w`/`h`.\n\nRun everything with `cd translation && bash tools/run_all.sh` (exits 0). `c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8167,"cache_read_input_tokens":79560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8167,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a675958-8a5c-4163-983a-1ededba583e3","uuid":"55360f1a-92b1-4209-9222-c2c92a58a111","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:39:08.834Z"}
